vhost-user-gpu: no read handler without a socket

gl_flushed re-arms the GPU socket's read handler whenever the display
reports a flush, also before the device started (or after it stopped), when
there is no socket (fd -1). With a SPICE client connected while the firmware
runs, QEMU then logged "failed to read msg header: 0, ..." on every flush until
the guest's driver started the device. Only arm it with a socket. Applies on
top of patch 0006.

--- a/hw/display/vhost-user-gpu.c
+++ b/hw/display/vhost-user-gpu.c
@@ -463,6 +463,14 @@
 static void
 vhost_user_gpu_update_blocked(VhostUserGPU *g, bool blocked)
 {
+    /*
+     * No socket before the device starts (or after it stopped): a GL display
+     * that reports a flush then (a SPICE client connected while the firmware
+     * runs) would have the handler read fd -1 ("failed to read msg header")
+     */
+    if (g->vhost_gpu_fd == -1) {
+        return;
+    }
     qemu_set_fd_handler(g->vhost_gpu_fd,
                         blocked ? NULL : vhost_user_gpu_chr_read, NULL, g);
 }
